  "canon:pmid": "24251212",
  "canon:title": "Renal rickets-practical approach.",
  "canon:abstract": "Rickets/osteomalacia is an important problem in a tropical country. Many cases are due to poor vitamin D intake or calcium deficient diets and can be corrected by administration of calcium and vitamin D. However, some cases are refractory to vitamin D therapy and are related to renal defects. These include rickets of renal tubular acidosis (RTA), hypophosphatemic rickets, and vitamin D dependent rickets (VDDR). The latter is due to impaired action of 1alpha-hydroxylase in renal tubule. These varieties need proper diagnosis and specific treatment. ",
  "canon:text": "Renal rickets-practical approach. Rickets/osteomalacia is an important problem in a tropical country. Many cases are due to poor vitamin D intake or calcium deficient diets and can be corrected by administration of calcium and vitamin D. However, some cases are refractory to vitamin D therapy and are related to renal defects. These include rickets of renal tubular acidosis (RTA), hypophosphatemic rickets, and vitamin D dependent rickets (VDDR). The latter is due to impaired action of 1alpha-hydroxylase in renal tubule. These varieties need proper diagnosis and specific treatment. ",
